  "flag_reading": [
    "A flag is kind:field:cause. Fields are the finding schema's names: cvss_base, composite_score, severity_band, remediation_sla, risk_disposition, review_date, reachability, cvss_vector.",
    "Step reading of D9's causes: a changed cvss_base is 'vector', a changed composite_score is 'arithmetic', a changed severity_band is 'band-mapping' (or 'rounding' for a tie), and a changed remediation_sla, risk_disposition or review_date is 'follows-band'. A change that the asset tags alone explain takes 'retagged' and the cause 'asset-tags' on every field it moves (ruling A).",
    "basis 'pinned': the flag string appears in ADR-050, the spec or the contracts. 'derived': composed from that grammar by the reading above. 'optional': the renderer may add it or not, and a test must accept both.",
    "A flag that the renderer adds and that is not listed is a defect of one side: the list is complete for the cases here."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Ruling B, PR 1: T-4 is a NEW finding whose ID the baseline's risk-scores.md already used for another finding (a tampering finding on vector-store-a, scored High, with a human owner and an Accept disposition). A NEW finding whose ID is in any baseline row goes to the agent, never to the carried set, and is flagged reused-id. Nothing of the old row may reach the new finding.",
    "T-5 is a NEW finding with a number the baseline never used: scored fresh, and not flagged. It is the control.",
    "agent_inputs holds the judgment that a scorer agent returns for T-4 and T-5 (the part payload's keys, with prose that has no digit). A test builds a tachi.part/1 from it for the planned batch. The expected values follow from it: a NEW finding in a baseline-aware run is held to its own category's bound (score_bounds, 6.1 to 8.1 for tampering), the owner is Unassigned, and the review date is this run's date plus the new SLA.",
    "I-1 is in Section 4c as RESOLVED and has a baseline row, which R-30 carries verbatim and marks resolved. It is not a reuse: its ID is not in Section 7.",
    "The PR 2 half of this variant (a baseline whose high-water mark sits above its live IDs) is T148's, in id-reuse/pr2/."
  ],
